--- a/packages/coding-agent/docs/tui.md
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/docs/tui.md
@@ -145,6 +145,8 @@ Finish the interaction with the completion callback supplied to the component fa
 
 For an inline detail view opened by an editor-border badge, pass `{ retainEditorBorders: true }` to `ctx.ui.custom()`. The editor's visible border widgets remain above/below the view, without showing the draft or moving keyboard focus to the hidden editor. A second badge click can call that interaction's completion callback to close it. Keep one pending/open interaction per badge and revoke its callback on session shutdown; repeated clicks must not stack duplicate views. Empty border rows take no space. The option is ignored for overlays and custom editors without `createBorderComponent()` support. Nested confirmation/input dialogs do not retain the rows. Mouse interaction requires fullscreen mode or regular mode with `regularMouse: true`; preserve command/shortcut and keyboard dismissal paths.
 
+In regular mode, retained inline views receive a bounded structural allocation after reserving the actual footer and below-editor widgets at the current width. Use `VStack` with fixed chrome (`shrink: 0`) and a shrinkable `ScrollView` body (`grow: 1, shrink: 1, minSize: 0`) so the body yields space to the retained badges. The allocation updates on resize and footer/widget changes; do not subtract those reservations again inside the view. Ordinary editors and custom views without this option keep their intrinsic rendering. This does not add regular-mode wheel-scroll defaults.
+
 See [`retained-border-details.ts`](../examples/extensions/retained-border-details.ts) for a repeat-click detail view with a command and keyboard dismissal path. See [`overlay-qa-tests.ts`](../examples/extensions/overlay-qa-tests.ts) for positioning, stacking, focus, responsive visibility, and animation behavior.
 
 ## Apply themes correctly
